Morning chill awakens you. Of course, the fire by the entrance is long gone. You're very lucky that nobody else was interested in you during the night.
Your friends sleep side by side in a row, embracing each other to keep warm. You wake them up. The hood of Irene's cloak is soiled in clay, Doyle's hair stands on end, but all in all, everyone is in good spirits.
After discussing once again what happened yesterday and eating a piece of bread found in the bag, you decide to keep going. It's time to get out of this forest.